name 'iterating-with-ai-postassessment-q8_2025'

question 'A filter function works by checking a "predicate." What is a predicate in this context?'

wrong 'A piece of code that adds two numbers together.'
right 'A true/false test applied to each item to determine if it should be included in the results.'
wrong 'The label at the top of a data column.'
wrong 'A button that resets the entire application.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 6

In filtering, a predicate is the condition (e.g., `price < 20`) that evaluates each item. If the predicate is true, the item is kept; if false, it is excluded.
MARKDOWN
